  "verbalization": "Mepyramine is linked to Allergic Rhinitis through a series of intermediate indications, all of which are classified under the broader category of Nasopharyngitis. This suggests that Mepyramine may exert its effects on the nasal mucosa, potentially modulating inflammatory pathways that are also involved in allergic responses. The presence of multiple overlapping indications—Nasopharyngitis, Chlorcyclizine, and Tramazoline—indicates a possible shared mechanism of action or a common pathway in the body that connects these drugs to allergic rhinitis. The consistent score of 0.4377 across the three paths suggests a plausible, though not yet fully elucidated, relationship between Mepyramine and the development of allergic rhinitis. The integration of these pathways highlights the potential for Mepyramine to influence inflammatory processes in the nasal region, which could contribute to the onset or severity of allergic rhinitis.",
